# Novopetrovskoye, Republic of Bashkortostan

}}
Novopetrovskoye () is a village (selo) in Zianchurinsky District of the Republic of Bashkortostan, Russia, located north of the Russian border with Kazakhstan and near Orsk. The population is small; some estimates suggest only a few hundred residents, around 700 according to unofficial figures.  The village mainly relies on traditional rural activities like farming and raising livestock, which is common in villages across Bashkortostan.
